Spec: Admin Frontend

Purpose:
  Native C++/Qt UI for managing and monitoring the MitM Data Aggregator.

Platform: C++

References:
  ../mitm-2.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Depends on:
  /admin/dashboard/stats

Must:
  Display DB information and DLQ cursor count on the dashboard (Issue #4).
  Avoid using hardcoded fallback authentication tokens.
  Manage object lifecycles safely to avoid use-after-free conditions.
  Sanitize all OS inputs, such as environment variables, before using them in file paths.
  Reduce the lifetime of secrets in memory and implement secure wiping for password/proxy buffers.
  Avoid passing proxy credentials as URL strings in plain text and prohibit dummy credentials.
  Handle API error responses, timeouts, and HTTP status codes (e.g., 401/403) uniformly via a central API client.
  Pin third-party dependencies (e.g., QXlsx) to verified release tags or commit hashes.
  Secure dependencies using lockfiles (SBOM) and regular vulnerability scanning.
  Establish CTest and CI pipelines for testing configuration, cryptography, and UI logic.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Remove the hardcoded fallback token in ConfigManager::GetAuthHeader.
  [x] #2 Fix the use-after-free risk in the update thread of the About dialog (MainWindow.cpp).
  [x] #3 Sanitize OS Username (USER/USERNAME) in configuration file paths to prevent path traversal.
  [ ] #4 Introduce a common API client module to uniformly handle HTTP status codes, schemas, timeouts, and error responses.
  [ ] #5 Implement secure memory wiping (e.g., sodium_memzero) for password and proxy buffers to reduce secret lifetime.
  [ ] #6 Refactor proxy credential handling to avoid plain text URL strings and reject unauthenticated dummy credentials.
  [ ] #7 Validate user roles before sensitive UI actions and prompt for re-authentication on 401/403 responses.
  [ ] #8 Pin the QXlsx dependency in CMake to a verified release tag or commit hash instead of tracking the master branch.
  [ ] #9 Setup CTest and Continuous Integration (CI) pipelines for core components (crypto, config, roles).
  [ ] #10 Introduce dependency lockfiles (SBOM) and regular vulnerability scanning.
  [ ] #11 Add telemetry for network latencies, API error rates, and update checks.
  [ ] #12 Consolidate secret management to align with the overall MitM Scheduler strategy.
  [x] #13 Feature: Issue #4 - Fetch and display dashboard stats from /admin/dashboard/stats
